      "readTime": "10 min",
      "tags": ["Color", "Production", "Figma"],
      "body": "<h2>The context problem</h2><p>You\u2019ve built a gorgeous palette. Then development starts and everything falls apart. Colors that were harmonious in your design file look flat, muddy, or clashing in the browser.</p><blockquote><p>Color has no meaning in isolation. Every color is changed by everything around it.</p></blockquote><h2>Simultaneous contrast</h2><p>Josef Albers demonstrated that color perception is entirely relational. A gray appears cool on a warm background and warm on a cool one. When you test a palette in a design file, you\u2019re testing it against white \u2014 the default background of every design tool.</p>"
