      "tags": ["Layout", "Composition", "Whitespace"],
      "body": "<h2>What fills the gaps</h2><p>Beginning designers fill space. Experienced designers do the opposite: they remove elements until what remains is essential, and then they work on the quality of what\u2019s left \u2014 the voids.</p><blockquote><p>In music, the rests are as important as the notes. In design, the space is as active as the form.</p></blockquote><h2>The figure-ground relationship</h2><p>Gestalt psychology gave us the vocabulary: figure and ground. The figure is the object we attend to; the ground is everything else. But ground is not passive \u2014 it can become figure.</p>"
