      "tags": ["Branding", "Logo", "Identity"],
      "body": "<h2>Cleverness is not meaning</h2><p>Today\u2019s design culture has confused clever with meaningful. The dual-meaning logo, the letterform hidden in negative space \u2014 these tricks abound, but most are forgotten within a year of launch.</p><blockquote><p>A logo is not a brand. It is a vessel that the brand fills over time.</p></blockquote><h2>What meaning actually is</h2><p>Meaning in a mark isn\u2019t encoded in the shape \u2014 it accumulates through use. The Nike swoosh meant nothing when it was designed in 1971.</p>"
