      "readTime": "7 min",
      "tags": ["Process", "Critique", "Feedback"],
      "body": "<h2>The failure of I like/I don\u2019t like</h2><p>Most design critique is conducted through preference. This feedback is nearly useless \u2014 it tells the designer nothing about why, and it conflates personal taste with design judgment.</p><blockquote><p>Good critique is generous: it assumes the designer made intelligent choices and asks what those choices were trying to achieve.</p></blockquote><h2>A criteria-based framework</h2><p>Effective critique is criteria-based. Before evaluating work, establish what the work is trying to accomplish \u2014 the problem it solves, the audience it serves, the constraints it operates within.</p>"
